{"timestamp":"2026-09-22T20:29:53.861Z","level":"info","event":"provider.together.response","fields":{"provider":"together","endpoint":"/chat/completions","response":{"httpStatus":200,"contentType":"text/event-stream","providerRequestId":"8375760d-aws_ec1","model":"moonshotai/Kimi-K3","text":"{\n  \"learningObjectives\": [\n    {\n      \"statement\": \"Distinguish between righteousness as a gift and the harvest of righteousness, and explain why both must be visible in a believer's life.\",\n      \"measurableVerb\": \"distinguish\",\n      \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"c963b0b0-1108-7ea7-940d-01123d9cc020\", \"7af22950-46db-75ef-a410-7afe128a90aa\", \"d0c0e6db-3dc0-7132-80b1-b30a86bfb826\"],\n      \"confidence\": 0.95\n    },\n    {\n      \"statement\": \"Identify the three ramifications of the Hebrew word Tzedakah and describe how each one applies to daily conduct.\",\n      \"measurableVerb\": \"identify\",\n      \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"06034497-9561-73ab-9a48-7e0b4dd07526\", \"74a62c36-c225-74cd-ab8b-4c70bfa21c0c\", \"fe3027da-43fa-7c54-abee-645434318ebe\", \"49c29e8f-988b-7974-8e1c-98507766b8dc\"],\n      \"confidence\": 0.95\n    },\n    {\n      \"statement\": \"Describe at least three Kingdom Economics practices from Biblical law and explain how each protects the vulnerable.\",\n      \"measurableVerb\": \"describe\",\n      \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"b29eff38-6707-7ec8-9cc2-3acf8b734309\", \"23d224bd-1662-7e5a-93b1-c26aa4216531\", \"f1f0308a-70b9-7c61-bf74-93a6bf2ad067\", \"a8294542-be65-7173-89e6-421f1913a466\", \"9192540a-67d8-7cd6-8b2a-7c756cd244d9\", \"b2b17cf5-d046-7435-b026-b9e3ddb02152\"],\n      \"confidence\": 0.92\n    },\n    {\n      \"statement\": \"Explain the difference between the power of God and the wisdom of God using the Jethro and Mark 5 examples, and predict what happens when wisdom does not follow power.\",\n      \"measurableVerb\": \"explain\",\n      \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"afe140a5-8141-7709-8e11-8dfb41acef12\", \"44fdb66c-c888-7231-9e57-293f33c4efea\", \"2f2a6065-ab09-75d0-b83d-f382b614cf54\"],\n      \"confidence\": 0.9\n    },\n    {\n      \"statement\": \"List the five pillars of financial stewardship and calculate a sample budget using the 50/30/20 allocation rule.\",\n      \"measurableVerb\": \"calculate\",\n      \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"f95b27d2-c234-738f-87ee-cf404117fd5a\", \"d8d10398-fc31-7207-8067-7d205b09e480\", \"dd8e865f-a031-7bdc-8f60-6","textChunks":["{\n  \"learningObjectives\": [\n    {\n      \"statement\": \"Distinguish between righteousness as a gift and the harvest of righteousness, and explain why both must be visible in a believer's life.\",\n      \"measurableVerb\": \"distinguish\",\n      \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"c963b0b0-1108-7ea7-940d-01123d9cc020\", \"7af22950-46db-75ef-a410-7afe128a90aa\", \"d0c0e6db-3dc0-7132-80b1-b30a86bfb826\"],\n      \"confidence\": 0.95\n    },\n    {\n      \"statement\": \"Identify the three ramifications of the Hebrew word Tzedakah and describe how each one applies to daily conduct.\",\n      \"measurableVerb\": \"identify\",\n      \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"06034497-9561-73ab-9a48-7e0b4dd07526\", \"74a62c36-c225-74cd-ab8b-4c70bfa21c0c\", \"fe3027da-43fa-7c54-abee-645434318ebe\", \"49c29e8f-988b-7974-8e1c-98507766b8dc\"],\n      \"confidence\": 0.95\n    },\n    {\n      \"statement\": \"Describe at least three Kingdom Economics practices from Biblical law and explain how each protects the vulnerable.\",\n      \"measurableVerb\": \"describe\",\n      \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"b29eff38-6707-7ec8-9cc2-3acf8b734309\", \"23d224bd-1662-7e5a-93b1-c26aa4216531\", \"f1f0308a-70b9-7c61-bf74-93a6bf2ad067\", \"a8294542-be65-7173-89e6-421f1913a466\", \"9192540a-67d8-7cd6-8b2a-7c756cd244d9\", \"b2b17cf5-d046-7435-b026-b9e3ddb02152\"],\n      \"confidence\": 0.92\n    },\n    {\n      \"statement\": \"Explain the difference between the power of God and the wisdom of God using the Jethro and Mark 5 examples, and predict what happens when wisdom does not follow power.\",\n      \"measurableVerb\": \"explain\",\n      \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"afe140a5-8141-7709-8e11-8dfb41acef12\", \"44fdb66c-c888-7231-9e57-293f33c4efea\", \"2f2a6065-ab09-75d0-b83d-f382b614cf54\"],\n      \"confidence\": 0.9\n    },\n    {\n      \"statement\": \"List the five pillars of financial stewardship and calculate a sample budget using the 50/30/20 allocation rule.\",\n      \"measurableVerb\": \"calculate\",\n      \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"f95b27d2-c234-738f-87ee-cf404117fd5a\", \"d8d10398-fc31-7207-8067-7d205b09e480\", \"dd8e865f-a031-7bdc-8f60-6","7cddffe293f\", \"19c878fa-239b-717b-b639-679449af7ad3\", \"7a32b18c-fe32-715f-b6f2-3ef07a0836cf\", \"66e311a8-add0-7a1d-8ef6-093444c88a60\", \"09df5ee4-b668-7289-9457-76279f00717b\"],\n      \"confidence\": 0.9\n    },\n    {\n      \"statement\": \"Compare the outcomes of the two servants in the Parable of the Talents and explain why the one-talent servant was condemned.\",\n      \"measurableVerb\": \"compare\",\n      \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"49ec6ab8-4041-757d-8594-ceb5170b4b8e\"],\n      \"confidence\": 0.88\n    }\n  ],\n  \"planningMetadata\": {\n    \"keyConcepts\": [\n      {\n        \"concept\": \"Two manifestations of righteousness: gift (positional) versus harvest (practical)\",\n        \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"c963b0b0-1108-7ea7-940d-01123d9cc020\", \"7af22950-46db-75ef-a410-7afe128a90aa\", \"d0c0e6db-3dc0-7132-80b1-b30a86bfb826\"]\n      },\n      {\n        \"concept\": \"Generosity as a willing overflow of righteousness rather than forced compliance\",\n        \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"19d141cb-9c20-7966-8416-afe5863ec966\"]\n      },\n      {\n        \"concept\": \"Tzedakah unites personal morality, justice, and charity into one whole\",\n        \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"06034497-9561-73ab-9a48-7e0b4dd07526\", \"74a62c36-c225-74cd-ab8b-4c70bfa21c0c\", \"fe3027da-43fa-7c54-abee-645434318ebe\", \"49c29e8f-988b-7974-8e1c-98507766b8dc\"]\n      },\n      {\n        \"concept\": \"Kingdom Economics laws: fairness over legal rights, debt cancellation, gleanings, prompt wages, refusing exploitation\",\n        \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"b29eff38-6707-7ec8-9cc2-3acf8b734309\", \"23d224bd-1662-7e5a-93b1-c26aa4216531\", \"f1f0308a-70b9-7c61-bf74-93a6bf2ad067\", \"a8294542-be65-7173-89e6-421f1913a466\", \"9192540a-67d8-7cd6-8b2a-7c756cd244d9\", \"b2b17cf5-d046-7435-b026-b9e3ddb02152\"]\n      },\n      {\n        \"concept\": \"Power produces the miracle; wisdom sustains it\",\n        \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"44fdb66c-c888-7231-9e57-293f33c4efea\", \"2f2a6065-ab09-75d0-b83d-f382b614cf54\"]\n      },\n      {\n        \"concept\": \"Stewardship: God gives the power to get wealth and demands acco","untability\",\n        \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"2e7f2eb1-2d9f-71fc-863c-14b5cea9acaf\", \"49ec6ab8-4041-757d-8594-ceb5170b4b8e\"]\n      },\n      {\n        \"concept\": \"Five pillars of financial faithfulness: budgeting/tracking, protection, savings, investment, debt management\",\n        \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"f95b27d2-c234-738f-87ee-cf404117fd5a\", \"d8d10398-fc31-7207-8067-7d205b09e480\", \"19c878fa-239b-717b-b639-679449af7ad3\", \"7a32b18c-fe32-715f-b6f2-3ef07a0836cf\", \"66e311a8-add0-7a1d-8ef6-093444c88a60\", \"09df5ee4-b668-7289-9457-76279f00717b\"]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"prerequisiteKnowledge\": [\n      {\n        \"item\": \"Basic familiarity with the Biblical narrative of David and Goliath and the roles of Goliath and King Saul\",\n        \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"c2a2b9c1-12af-73f2-84f0-432fe91a4b6a\"]\n      },\n      {\n        \"item\": \"Awareness that the sermons draw on specific scriptures such as Proverbs 8:18, 2 Corinthians 9, and Acts 20:32\",\n        \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"1259c33f-c13b-733f-a31b-eac5bd884c63\", \"56a5c45d-a5ef-700a-a272-89b5569a62ea\", \"19d141cb-9c20-7966-8416-afe5863ec966\"]\n      },\n      {\n        \"item\": \"General understanding of money terms used in the sermons such as income, expenses, debt, savings, and interest\",\n        \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"49ec6ab8-4041-757d-8594-ceb5170b4b8e\", \"dd8e865f-a031-7bdc-8f60-67cddffe293f\", \"09df5ee4-b668-7289-9457-76279f00717b\"]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"vocabulary\": [\n      {\n        \"term\": \"Positional Righteousness\",\n        \"definition\": \"Righteousness received as a gift by grace through faith, a fixed legal credit that cannot be increased or diminished.\",\n        \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"7af22950-46db-75ef-a410-7afe128a90aa\"]\n      },\n      {\n        \"term\": \"Harvest of Righteousness\",\n        \"definition\": \"The dynamic, visible fruits and works of righteousness before people, which can and should be multiplied.\",\n        \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"d0c0e6db-3dc0-7132-80b1-b30a86bfb826\"]\n      },\n      {\n        \"term\": \"Tzedakah\",\n        \"definition\": \"The Hebr","ew word (T-Z-E-D-A-K-A-H) that treats morality, justice, and charity as inseparable parts of one whole.\",\n        \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"06034497-9561-73ab-9a48-7e0b4dd07526\"]\n      },\n      {\n        \"term\": \"Sowing Sparingly\",\n        \"definition\": \"Giving out of reluctant compulsion or exhaustion, lacking excitement or love; a state of the giver's heart, not just an amount.\",\n        \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"19d141cb-9c20-7966-8416-afe5863ec966\"]\n      },\n      {\n        \"term\": \"Gleanings\",\n        \"definition\": \"The corners and unharvested produce left in fields for the poor, the widow, and the stranger as a built-in safety net.\",\n        \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"a8294542-be65-7173-89e6-421f1913a466\"]\n      },\n      {\n        \"term\": \"Steward\",\n        \"definition\": \"A manager of God's property rather than an independent owner; in the Kingdom economy, owners are treated as rebels.\",\n        \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"2e7f2eb1-2d9f-71fc-863c-14b5cea9acaf\"]\n      },\n      {\n        \"term\": \"Budget\",\n        \"definition\": \"A written plan for your money before it arrives.\",\n        \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"d8d10398-fc31-7207-8067-7d205b09e480\"]\n      },\n      {\n        \"term\": \"50/30/20 Rule\",\n        \"definition\": \"An allocation formula: 50% needs, 30% wants, 20% savings and investment, with savings growing as income grows.\",\n        \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"dd8e865f-a031-7bdc-8f60-67cddffe293f\"]\n      },\n      {\n        \"term\": \"Emergency Fund\",\n        \"definition\": \"A liquid reserve of 3 to 6 months of living expenses that prevents breaking long-term investments in a crisis.\",\n        \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"19c878fa-239b-717b-b639-679449af7ad3\", \"dbdda288-96d0-79a1-acf2-e6a27600477d\"]\n      },\n      {\n        \"term\": \"Risk Tolerance\",\n        \"definition\": \"The level of investment risk a person can handle, which must be understood by investing in knowledge before investing money.\",\n        \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"66e311a8-add0-7a1d-8ef6-093444c88a60\"]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"misconceptions\": [\n      {","\n        \"misconception\": \"Because righteousness is a gift, works are unnecessary.\",\n        \"correction\": \"The gift of righteousness is fixed, but the harvest of righteousness must be multiplied; works do not qualify us before God but demonstrate faith before people.\",\n        \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"d0c0e6db-3dc0-7132-80b1-b30a86bfb826\", \"c2a2b9c1-12af-73f2-84f0-432fe91a4b6a\"]\n      },\n      {\n        \"misconception\": \"Sowing sparingly is only about giving a small amount of money.\",\n        \"correction\": \"Sowing sparingly describes the state of the giver's heart—reluctant compulsion or exhaustion—not merely the financial quantity.\",\n        \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"19d141cb-9c20-7966-8416-afe5863ec966\"]\n      },\n      {\n        \"misconception\": \"Giving to the poor is optional benevolence.\",\n        \"correction\": \"In the Hebrew scriptures, giving to the poor is classified as justice and righteousness; withholding help when you have power to give violates Tzedakah.\",\n        \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"49c29e8f-988b-7974-8e1c-98507766b8dc\"]\n      },\n      {\n        \"misconception\": \"Having the power of God is enough to sustain a blessed life.\",\n        \"correction\": \"Power and wisdom are distinct yet both necessary; without wisdom to organize and structure, a person will burn out and destroy what was built—power produces the miracle, wisdom sustains it.\",\n        \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"44fdb66c-c888-7231-9e57-293f33c4efea\", \"2f2a6065-ab09-75d0-b83d-f382b614cf54\"]\n      },\n      {\n        \"misconception\": \"A bigger amount of money will solve money problems.\",\n        \"correction\": \"Your current financial level is a stewardship test; if you cannot manage 200,000 naira, 20 million will only enable more expensive mistakes.\",\n        \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"49ec6ab8-4041-757d-8594-ceb5170b4b8e\"]\n      },\n      {\n        \"misconception\": \"Leaving money in a bank account is a safe investment strategy.\",\n        \"correction\": \"Inflation and bank maintenance fees and levies slowly deplete idle capi","tal; investment requires first investing in knowledge and understanding risk.\",\n        \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"66e311a8-add0-7a1d-8ef6-093444c88a60\"]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"assessmentQuestions\": [\n      {\n        \"question\": \"In your own words, what is the difference between righteousness as a gift and the harvest of righteousness?\",\n        \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"7af22950-46db-75ef-a410-7afe128a90aa\", \"d0c0e6db-3dc0-7132-80b1-b30a86bfb826\"]\n      },\n      {\n        \"question\": \"Name the three ramifications of Tzedakah and give one everyday example of each.\",\n        \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"06034497-9561-73ab-9a48-7e0b4dd07526\", \"74a62c36-c225-74cd-ab8b-4c70bfa21c0c\", \"fe3027da-43fa-7c54-abee-645434318ebe\", \"49c29e8f-988b-7974-8e1c-98507766b8dc\"]\n      },\n      {\n        \"question\": \"Choose two Kingdom Economics laws from the sermon and explain how each one protects poor or vulnerable people.\",\n        \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"23d224bd-1662-7e5a-93b1-c26aa4216531\", \"f1f0308a-70b9-7c61-bf74-93a6bf2ad067\", \"a8294542-be65-7173-89e6-421f1913a466\", \"9192540a-67d8-7cd6-8b2a-7c756cd244d9\", \"b2b17cf5-d046-7435-b026-b9e3ddb02152\"]\n      },\n      {\n        \"question\": \"After Jesus raised Jairus's daughter, why did He command that she be given something to eat, and what does this teach about money management?\",\n        \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"2f2a6065-ab09-75d0-b83d-f382b614cf54\"]\n      },\n      {\n        \"question\": \"If your monthly income is 100,000 naira, use the 50/30/20 rule to calculate how much should go to needs, wants, and savings/investment.\",\n        \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"dd8e865f-a031-7bdc-8f60-67cddffe293f\"]\n      },\n      {\n        \"question\": \"Why was the one-talent servant condemned even though he did not lose the money?\",\n        \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"49ec6ab8-4041-757d-8594-ceb5170b4b8e\"]\n      }\n    ]\n  }\n}"],"textChunksTruncated":false,"textCharacters":11820,"reasoningCharacters":0,"finishReason":"stop","inputTokens":"[REDACTED]","outputTokens":"[REDACTED]"},"retries":0,"latencyMs":39984,"service":"pipeline-worker","correlationId":"01a0cace-ea97-723d-94ff-2a8bbd8c6e24"}}
