",\"verb\":\"calculate\",\"sourceBlockIds\":[\"f95b27d2-c234-738f-87ee-cf404117fd5a\",\"d8d10398-fc31-7207-8067-7d205b09e480\",\"dd8e865f-a031-7bdc-8f60-67cddffe293f\",\"19c878fa-239b-717b-b639-679449af7ad3\",\"7a32b18c-fe32-715f-b6f2-3ef07a0836cf\",\"66e311a8-add0-7a1d-8ef6-093444c88a60\",\"09df5ee4-b668-7289-9457-76279f00717b\"],\"confidence\":0.9},{\"statement\":\"Compare the outcomes of the servants in","textChunks":["{\"schemaVersion\":\"objectives-v1\",\"objectives\":[{\"statement\":\"Distinguish between righteousness as a gift and the harvest of righteousness, and explain why both must be visible in a believer's life.\",\"verb\":\"distinguish\",\"sourceBlockIds\":[\"c963b0b0-1108-7ea7-940d-01123d9cc020\",\"7af22950-46db-75ef-a410-7afe128a90aa\",\"d0c0e6db-3dc0-7132-80b1-b30a86bfb826\"],\"confidence\":0.95},{\"statement\":\"Identify the three ramifications of the Hebrew word Tzedakah and describe how each one applies to daily conduct.\",\"verb\":\"identify\",\"sourceBlockIds\":[\"06034497-9561-73ab-9a48-7e0b4dd07526\",\"74a62c36-c225-74cd-ab8b-4c70bfa21c0c\",\"fe3027da-43fa-7c54-abee-645434318ebe\",\"49c29e8f-988b-7974-8e1c-98507766b8dc\"],\"confidence\":0.95},{\"statement\":\"Describe at least three Kingdom Economics practices from Biblical law and explain how each protects the vulnerable.\",\"verb\":\"describe\",\"sourceBlockIds\":[\"b29eff38-6707-7ec8-9cc2-3acf8b734309\",\"23d224bd-1662-7e5a-93b1-c26aa4216531\",\"f1f0308a-70b9-7c61-bf74-93a6bf2ad067\",\"a8294542-be65-7173-89e6-421f1913a466\",\"9192540a-67d8-7cd6-8b2a-7c756cd244d9\",\"b2b17cf5-d046-7435-b026-b9e3ddb02152\"],\"confidence\":0.92},{\"statement\":\"Explain the difference between the power of God and the wisdom of God using the Jethro and Mark 5 examples, and predict what happens when wisdom does not follow power.\",\"verb\":\"explain\",\"sourceBlockIds\":[\"afe140a5-8141-7709-8e11-8dfb41acef12\",\"44fdb66c-c888-7231-9e57-293f33c4efea\",\"2f2a6065-ab09-75d0-b83d-f382b614cf54\"],\"confidence\":0.9},{\"statement\":\"List the five pillars of financial stewardship and calculate a sample budget using the 50/30/20 allocation rule.\",\"verb\":\"calculate\",\"sourceBlockIds\":[\"f95b27d2-c234-738f-87ee-cf404117fd5a\",\"d8d10398-fc31-7207-8067-7d205b09e480\",\"dd8e865f-a031-7bdc-8f60-67cddffe293f\",\"19c878fa-239b-717b-b639-679449af7ad3\",\"7a32b18c-fe32-715f-b6f2-3ef07a0836cf\",\"66e311a8-add0-7a1d-8ef6-093444c88a60\",\"09df5ee4-b668-7289-9457-76279f00717b\"],\"confidence\":0.9},{\"statement\":\"Compare the outcomes of the servants in"," the Parable of the Talents and explain why the one-talent servant was condemned.\",\"verb\":\"compare\",\"sourceBlockIds\":[\"49ec6ab8-4041-757d-8594-ceb5170b4b8e\"],\"confidence\":0.88}],\"keyConcepts\":[{\"text\":\"Two manifestations of righteousness: gift (positional) versus harvest (practical)\",\"sourceBlockIds\":[\"c963b0b0-1108-7ea7-940d-01123d9cc020\",\"7af22950-46db-75ef-a410-7afe128a90aa\",\"d0c0e6db-3dc0-7132-80b1-b30a86bfb826\"]},{\"text\":\"Generosity as a willing overflow of righteousness rather than forced compliance\",\"sourceBlockIds\":[\"19d141cb-9c20-7966-8416-afe5863ec966\"]},{\"text\":\"Tzedakah unites personal morality, justice, and charity into one whole\",\"sourceBlockIds\":[\"06034497-9561-73ab-9a48-7e0b4dd07526\",\"74a62c36-c225-74cd-ab8b-4c70bfa21c0c\",\"fe3027da-43fa-7c54-abee-645434318ebe\",\"49c29e8f-988b-7974-8e1c-98507766b8dc\"]},{\"text\":\"Kingdom Economics laws: fairness over legal rights, debt cancellation, gleanings, prompt wages, refusing exploitation\",\"sourceBlockIds\":[\"b29eff38-6707-7ec8-9cc2-3acf8b734309\",\"23d224bd-1662-7e5a-93b1-c26aa4216531\",\"f1f0308a-70b9-7c61-bf74-93a6bf2ad067\",\"a8294542-be65-7173-89e6-421f1913a466\",\"9192540a-67d8-7cd6-8b2a-7c756cd244d9\",\"b2b17cf5-d046-7435-b026-b9e3ddb02152\"]},{\"text\":\"Power produces the miracle; wisdom sustains it\",\"sourceBlockIds\":[\"44fdb66c-c888-7231-9e57-293f33c4efea\",\"2f2a6065-ab09-75d0-b83d-f382b614cf54\"]},{\"text\":\"Stewardship: God gives the power to get wealth and demands accountability\",\"sourceBlockIds\":[\"2e7f2eb1-2d9f-71fc-863c-14b5cea9acaf\",\"49ec6ab8-4041-757d-8594-ceb5170b4b8e\"]},{\"text\":\"Five pillars of financial faithfulness: budgeting/tracking, protection, savings, investment, debt management\",\"sourceBlockIds\":[\"f95b27d2-c234-738f-87ee-cf404117fd5a\",\"d8d10398-fc31-7207-8067-7d205b09e480\",\"19c878fa-239b-717b-b639-679449af7ad3\",\"7a32b18c-fe32-715f-b6f2-3ef07a0836cf\",\"66e311a8-add0-7a1d-8ef6-093444c88a60\",\"09df5ee4-b668-7289-9457-76279f00717b\"]}],\"prerequisiteKnowledge\":[{\"text\":\"Basic familiarity with the Biblical narrative"," of David and Goliath and the roles of Goliath and King Saul\",\"sourceBlockIds\":[\"c2a2b9c1-12af-73f2-84f0-432fe91a4b6a\"]},{\"text\":\"Awareness that the sermons draw on specific scriptures such as Proverbs 8:18, 2 Corinthians 9, and Acts 20:32\",\"sourceBlockIds\":[\"1259c33f-c13b-733f-a31b-eac5bd884c63\",\"56a5c45d-a5ef-700a-a272-89b5569a62ea\",\"19d141cb-9c20-7966-8416-afe5863ec966\"]},{\"text\":\"General understanding of money terms used in the sermons such as income, expenses, debt, savings, and interest\",\"sourceBlockIds\":[\"49ec6ab8-4041-757d-8594-ceb5170b4b8e\",\"dd8e865f-a031-7bdc-8f60-67cddffe293f\",\"09df5ee4-b668-7289-9457-76279f00717b\"]}],\"vocabulary\":[{\"term\":\"Positional Righteousness\",\"definition\":\"Righteousness received as a gift by grace through faith, a fixed legal credit that cannot be increased or diminished.\",\"sourceBlockIds\":[\"7af22950-46db-75ef-a410-7afe128a90aa\"]},{\"term\":\"Harvest of Righteousness\",\"definition\":\"The dynamic, visible fruits and works of righteousness before people, which can and should be multiplied.\",\"sourceBlockIds\":[\"d0c0e6db-3dc0-7132-80b1-b30a86bfb826\"]},{\"term\":\"Tzedakah\",\"definition\":\"The Hebrew word (T-Z-E-D-A-K-A-H) that treats morality, justice, and charity as inseparable parts of one whole.\",\"sourceBlockIds\":[\"06034497-9561-73ab-9a48-7e0b4dd07526\"]},{\"term\":\"Sowing Sparingly\",\"definition\":\"Giving out of reluctant compulsion or exhaustion, lacking excitement or love; a state of the giver's heart, not just an amount.\",\"sourceBlockIds\":[\"19d141cb-9c20-7966-8416-afe5863ec966\"]},{\"term\":\"Gleanings\",\"definition\":\"The corners and unharvested produce left in fields for the poor, the widow, and the stranger as a built-in safety net.\",\"sourceBlockIds\":[\"a8294542-be65-7173-89e6-421f1913a466\"]},{\"term\":\"Steward\",\"definition\":\"A manager of God's property rather than an independent owner; in the Kingdom economy, owners are treated as rebels.\",\"sourceBlockIds\":[\"2e7f2eb1-2d9f-71fc-863c-14b5cea9acaf\"]},{\"term\":\"Budget\",\"definition\":\"A written plan for yo","ur money before it arrives.\",\"sourceBlockIds\":[\"d8d10398-fc31-7207-8067-7d205b09e480\"]},{\"term\":\"50/30/20 Rule\",\"definition\":\"An allocation formula: 50% needs, 30% wants, 20% savings and investment, with savings growing as income grows.\",\"sourceBlockIds\":[\"dd8e865f-a031-7bdc-8f60-67cddffe293f\"]},{\"term\":\"Emergency Fund\",\"definition\":\"A liquid reserve of 3 to 6 months of living expenses that prevents breaking long-term investments in a crisis.\",\"sourceBlockIds\":[\"19c878fa-239b-717b-b639-679449af7ad3\",\"dbdda288-96d0-79a1-acf2-e6a27600477d\"]},{\"term\":\"Risk Tolerance\",\"definition\":\"The level of investment risk a person can handle, which must be understood by investing in knowledge before investing money.\",\"sourceBlockIds\":[\"66e311a8-add0-7a1d-8ef6-093444c88a60\"]}],\"misconceptions\":[{\"misconception\":\"Because righteousness is a gift, works are unnecessary.\",\"correction\":\"The gift of righteousness is fixed, but the harvest of righteousness must be multiplied; works do not qualify us before God but demonstrate faith before people.\",\"sourceBlockIds\":[\"d0c0e6db-3dc0-7132-80b1-b30a86bfb826\",\"c2a2b9c1-12af-73f2-84f0-432fe91a4b6a\"]},{\"misconception\":\"Sowing sparingly is only about giving a small amount of money.\",\"correction\":\"Sowing sparingly describes the state of the giver's heart-reluctant compulsion or exhaustion-not merely the financial quantity.\",\"sourceBlockIds\":[\"19d141cb-9c20-7966-8416-afe5863ec966\"]},{\"misconception\":\"Giving to the poor is optional benevolence.\",\"correction\":\"In the Hebrew scriptures, giving to the poor is classified as justice and righteousness; withholding help when you have power to give violates Tzedakah.\",\"sourceBlockIds\":[\"49c29e8f-988b-7974-8e1c-98507766b8dc\"]},{\"misconception\":\"Having the power of God is enough to sustain a blessed life.\",\"correction\":\"Power and wisdom are distinct yet both necessary; without wisdom to organize and structure, a person will burn out and destroy what was built-power produces the miracle, wisdom sustains it.\",\"so","urceBlockIds\":[\"44fdb66c-c888-7231-9e57-293f33c4efea\",\"2f2a6065-ab09-75d0-b83d-f382b614cf54\"]},{\"misconception\":\"A bigger amount of money will solve money problems.\",\"correction\":\"Your current financial level is a stewardship test; if you cannot manage 200,000 naira, 20 million will only enable more expensive mistakes.\",\"sourceBlockIds\":[\"49ec6ab8-4041-757d-8594-ceb5170b4b8e\"]},{\"misconception\":\"Leaving money in a bank account is a safe investment strategy.\",\"correction\":\"Inflation and bank maintenance fees and levies slowly deplete idle capital; investment requires first investing in knowledge and understanding risk.\",\"sourceBlockIds\":[\"66e311a8-add0-7a1d-8ef6-093444c88a60\"]}],\"assessmentQuestions\":[{\"question\":\"In your own words, what is the difference between righteousness as a gift and the harvest of righteousness?\",\"sourceBlockIds\":[\"7af22950-46db-75ef-a410-7afe128a90aa\",\"d0c0e6db-3dc0-7132-80b1-b30a86bfb826\"]},{\"question\":\"Name the three ramifications of Tzedakah and give one everyday example of each.\",\"sourceBlockIds\":[\"06034497-9561-73ab-9a48-7e0b4dd07526\",\"74a62c36-c225-74cd-ab8b-4c70bfa21c0c\",\"fe3027da-43fa-7c54-abee-645434318ebe\",\"49c29e8f-988b-7974-8e1c-98507766b8dc\"]},{\"question\":\"Choose two Kingdom Economics laws from the sermon and explain how each one protects poor or vulnerable people.\",\"sourceBlockIds\":[\"23d224bd-1662-7e5a-93b1-c26aa4216531\",\"f1f0308a-70b9-7c61-bf74-93a6bf2ad067\",\"a8294542-be65-7173-89e6-421f1913a466\",\"9192540a-67d8-7cd6-8b2a-7c756cd244d9\",\"b2b17cf5-d046-7435-b026-b9e3ddb02152\"]},{\"question\":\"After Jesus raised Jairus's daughter, why did He command that she be given something to eat, and what does this teach about money management?\",\"sourceBlockIds\":[\"2f2a6065-ab09-75d0-b83d-f382b614cf54\"]},{\"question\":\"If your monthly income is 100,000 naira, use the 50/30/20 rule to calculate how much should go to needs, wants, and savings/investment.\",\"sourceBlockIds\":[\"dd8e865f-a031-7bdc-8f60-67cddffe293f\"]},{\"question\":\"Why was the one-talent ","servant condemned even though he did not lose the money?\",\"sourceBlockIds\":[\"49ec6ab8-4041-757d-8594-ceb5170b4b8e\"]}]}"],"textChunksTruncated":false,"textCharacters":10118,"reasoningCharacters":0,"finishReason":"stop","inputTokens":"[REDACTED]","outputTokens":"[REDACTED]"},"retries":0,"latencyMs":43290,"service":"pipeline-worker","correlationId":"01a0cace-ea97-723d-94ff-2a8bbd8c6e24"}}
