{"timestamp":"2026-09-22T20:32:38.650Z","level":"info","event":"provider.together.response","fields":{"provider":"together","endpoint":"/chat/completions","response":{"httpStatus":200,"contentType":"text/event-stream","providerRequestId":"f21e2fce-aws_ec1","model":"moonshotai/Kimi-K3","text":"{\"schemaVersion\":\"outline-v1\",\"targetDurationSeconds\":180,\"items\":[{\"kind\":\"hook\",\"title\":\"Two Miracles, One Meal\",\"description\":\"Open with the arresting contrast between two moments of power: Moses parting the Red Sea and Jesus raising a girl from the dead, followed by surprisingly ordinary instructions about work structure and a meal. This frames the lesson's big question: why does power always need wisdom to sustain it?\",\"objectiveIds\":[\"01a0cace-ecd7-7a1a-9412-52d954644606\"],\"sourceBlockIds\":[\"afe140a5-8141-7709-8e11-8dfb41acef12\",\"2f2a6065-ab09-75d0-b83d-f382b614cf54\"],\"estimatedSeconds\":18},{\"kind\":\"concept\",\"title\":\"Power vs. Wisdom: Jethro and Mark 5\",\"description\":\"Teach the distinction between the power of God and the wisdom of God using the Jethro narrative (Exodus 18:14-20), where Moses had miracle-working power but an unsustainable structure, and Mark 5:41-43, where Jesus followed resurrection power with the practical wisdom of food. Learners predict what happens when wisdom does not follow power: burnout, loss, and the undoing of what was built.\",\"objectiveIds\":[\"01a0cace-ecd7-7a1a-9412-52d954644606\"],\"sourceBlockIds\":[\"afe140a5-8141-7709-8e11-8dfb41acef12\",\"44fdb66c-c888-7231-9e57-293f33c4efea\",\"2f2a6065-ab09-75d0-b83d-f382b614cf54\"],\"estimatedSeconds\":30},{\"kind\":\"concept\",\"title\":\"Righteousness: Gift and Harvest\",\"description\":\"Explain the two manifestations of righteousness: the gift of righteousness, a fixed legal credit received by grace through faith (Galatians 3:6, Romans 4), and the harvest of righteousness, which is dynamic and can be multiplied (2 Corinthians 9:10). Emphasize why both must be visible: works do not qualify us before God, but they demonstrate our faith before people.\",\"objectiveIds\":[\"01a0cace-ecd7-7355-b1db-e3dafa507991\"],\"sourceBlockIds\":[\"c963b0b0-1108-7ea7-940d-01123d9cc020\",\"7af22950-46db-75ef-a410-7afe128a90aa\",\"d0c0e6db-3dc0-7132-80b1-b30a86bfb826\"],\"estimatedSeconds\":28},{\"kind\":\"concept\",\"title\":\"Tzedakah: One Word, T","textChunks":["{\"schemaVersion\":\"outline-v1\",\"targetDurationSeconds\":180,\"items\":[{\"kind\":\"hook\",\"title\":\"Two Miracles, One Meal\",\"description\":\"Open with the arresting contrast between two moments of power: Moses parting the Red Sea and Jesus raising a girl from the dead, followed by surprisingly ordinary instructions about work structure and a meal. This frames the lesson's big question: why does power always need wisdom to sustain it?\",\"objectiveIds\":[\"01a0cace-ecd7-7a1a-9412-52d954644606\"],\"sourceBlockIds\":[\"afe140a5-8141-7709-8e11-8dfb41acef12\",\"2f2a6065-ab09-75d0-b83d-f382b614cf54\"],\"estimatedSeconds\":18},{\"kind\":\"concept\",\"title\":\"Power vs. Wisdom: Jethro and Mark 5\",\"description\":\"Teach the distinction between the power of God and the wisdom of God using the Jethro narrative (Exodus 18:14-20), where Moses had miracle-working power but an unsustainable structure, and Mark 5:41-43, where Jesus followed resurrection power with the practical wisdom of food. Learners predict what happens when wisdom does not follow power: burnout, loss, and the undoing of what was built.\",\"objectiveIds\":[\"01a0cace-ecd7-7a1a-9412-52d954644606\"],\"sourceBlockIds\":[\"afe140a5-8141-7709-8e11-8dfb41acef12\",\"44fdb66c-c888-7231-9e57-293f33c4efea\",\"2f2a6065-ab09-75d0-b83d-f382b614cf54\"],\"estimatedSeconds\":30},{\"kind\":\"concept\",\"title\":\"Righteousness: Gift and Harvest\",\"description\":\"Explain the two manifestations of righteousness: the gift of righteousness, a fixed legal credit received by grace through faith (Galatians 3:6, Romans 4), and the harvest of righteousness, which is dynamic and can be multiplied (2 Corinthians 9:10). Emphasize why both must be visible: works do not qualify us before God, but they demonstrate our faith before people.\",\"objectiveIds\":[\"01a0cace-ecd7-7355-b1db-e3dafa507991\"],\"sourceBlockIds\":[\"c963b0b0-1108-7ea7-940d-01123d9cc020\",\"7af22950-46db-75ef-a410-7afe128a90aa\",\"d0c0e6db-3dc0-7132-80b1-b30a86bfb826\"],\"estimatedSeconds\":28},{\"kind\":\"concept\",\"title\":\"Tzedakah: One Word, T","hree Ramifications\",\"description\":\"Introduce the Hebrew word Tzedakah and its three inseparable ramifications: personal morality (standing clean before God, refusing to lie or steal), justice (refusing to oppress the vulnerable, acting uprightly in all transactions), and charity/generosity (giving to the poor as a matter of justice, not optional benevolence). Connect each ramification to daily conduct.\",\"objectiveIds\":[\"01a0cace-ecd7-7970-8683-661a513bb105\"],\"sourceBlockIds\":[\"06034497-9561-73ab-9a48-7e0b4dd07526\",\"74a62c36-c225-74cd-ab8b-4c70bfa21c0c\",\"fe3027da-43fa-7c54-abee-645434318ebe\",\"49c29e8f-988b-7974-8e1c-98507766b8dc\"],\"estimatedSeconds\":26},{\"kind\":\"example\",\"title\":\"Kingdom Economics in Practice\",\"description\":\"Walk through concrete Kingdom Economics practices from Biblical law and show how each protects the vulnerable: returning a poor debtor's cloak before sundown (Deuteronomy 24:10-13), periodic debt cancellation in the seventh year, leaving gleanings for the poor, prompt payment of workers (Jeremiah 22:13, James 5:4), and refusing to exploit bargaining power (Proverbs 22:22-23).\",\"objectiveIds\":[\"01a0cace-ecd7-7b8d-9e03-abc39630db01\"],\"sourceBlockIds\":[\"b29eff38-6707-7ec8-9cc2-3acf8b734309\",\"23d224bd-1662-7e5a-93b1-c26aa4216531\",\"f1f0308a-70b9-7c61-bf74-93a6bf2ad067\",\"a8294542-be65-7173-89e6-421f1913a466\",\"9192540a-67d8-7cd6-8b2a-7c756cd244d9\",\"b2b17cf5-d046-7435-b026-b9e3ddb02152\"],\"estimatedSeconds\":30},{\"kind\":\"concept\",\"title\":\"The Five Pillars and the 50/30/20 Rule\",\"description\":\"List the five pillars of financial stewardship: budgeting and tracking, protection, savings, investment, and debt management. Then work a sample budget using the 50/30/20 allocation rule: 50% needs, 30% wants, 20% savings and investment, noting that the savings share must grow as income grows.\",\"objectiveIds\":[\"01a0cace-ecd7-7239-afef-9a0413bb4e1c\"],\"sourceBlockIds\":[\"f95b27d2-c234-738f-87ee-cf404117fd5a\",\"d8d10398-fc31-7207-8067-7d205b09e480\",\"dd8e865f-a031-7bdc-8f60","-67cddffe293f\",\"19c878fa-239b-717b-b639-679449af7ad3\",\"7a32b18c-fe32-715f-b6f2-3ef07a0836cf\",\"66e311a8-add0-7a1d-8ef6-093444c88a60\",\"09df5ee4-b668-7289-9457-76279f00717b\"],\"estimatedSeconds\":30},{\"kind\":\"example\",\"title\":\"The Parable of the Talents\",\"description\":\"Compare the outcomes of the three servants in Matthew 25: the five-talent and two-talent servants grew what they were given, while the one-talent servant was condemned as 'wicked and lazy' not for earning less, but for making no interest and showing zero growth. Draw the lesson that the master expected the same standard of faithfulness from everyone, and that your current financial level is a stewardship test.\",\"objectiveIds\":[\"01a0cace-ecd7-7bc6-ae8b-1812d9d98dc6\"],\"sourceBlockIds\":[\"49ec6ab8-4041-757d-8594-ceb5170b4b8e\"],\"estimatedSeconds\":18},{\"kind\":\"summary\",\"title\":\"Power Sustained by Wisdom\",\"description\":\"Close by tying the thread together: power produces the miracle, wisdom sustains it. Righteousness is both a gift received and a harvest multiplied; Tzedakah fuses morality, justice, and generosity; Kingdom Economics protects the vulnerable; and faithful stewardship means budgeting, protecting, saving, investing, and managing debt with accountability, just as the faithful servants did.\",\"objectiveIds\":[\"01a0cace-ecd7-7a1a-9412-52d954644606\",\"01a0cace-ecd7-7355-b1db-e3dafa507991\",\"01a0cace-ecd7-7970-8683-661a513bb105\",\"01a0cace-ecd7-7b8d-9e03-abc39630db01\",\"01a0cace-ecd7-7239-afef-9a0413bb4e1c\",\"01a0cace-ecd7-7bc6-ae8b-1812d9d98dc6\"],\"sourceBlockIds\":[\"44fdb66c-c888-7231-9e57-293f33c4efea\",\"d0c0e6db-3dc0-7132-80b1-b30a86bfb826\",\"06034497-9561-73ab-9a48-7e0b4dd07526\",\"b29eff38-6707-7ec8-9cc2-3acf8b734309\",\"f95b27d2-c234-738f-87ee-cf404117fd5a\",\"49ec6ab8-4041-757d-8594-ceb5170b4b8e\"],\"estimatedSeconds\":20}]}"],"textChunksTruncated":false,"textCharacters":5803,"reasoningCharacters":0,"finishReason":"stop","inputTokens":"[REDACTED]","outputTokens":"[REDACTED]"},"retries":0,"latencyMs":25364,"service":"pipeline-worker","correlationId":"01a0cad1-a556-7a65-ad45-27a0f0b7e96f"}}
