{"timestamp":"2026-09-22T20:33:31.105Z","level":"info","event":"provider.together.response","fields":{"provider":"together","endpoint":"/chat/completions","response":{"httpStatus":200,"contentType":"text/event-stream","providerRequestId":"a9503521-aws_ec1","model":"moonshotai/Kimi-K3","text":"\n{\n  \"schemaVersion\": \"outline-v1\",\n  \"targetDurationSeconds\": 180,\n  \"items\": [\n    {\n      \"kind\": \"hook\",\n      \"title\": \"The 50/30/20 Challenge\",\n      \"description\": \"Open with a provocative question: 'If you received 20 million naira today, would you know exactly how to allocate it using the 50/30/20 rule, or would you simply make more expensive mistakes?' This frames the lesson's exploration of financial stewardship and Kingdom Economics.\",\n      \"objectiveIds\": [\"01a0cace-ecd7-7239-afef-9a0413bb4e1c\"],\n      \"sourceBlockIds\": [],\n      \"estimatedSeconds\": 25,\n      \"framingNote\": \"Generated framing device to engage learners by connecting the abstract concept of stewardship to a concrete financial scenario. Not directly sourced from the material.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"kind\": \"concept\",\n      \"title\": \"Righteousness: Gift vs. Harvest\",\n      \"description\": \"Distinguish between positional righteousness (a fixed gift received by grace through faith) and practical righteousness (the harvest of visible works that can be multiplied). Explain why both must be active in a believer's life to avoid doctrinal imbalance.\",\n      \"objectiveIds\": [\"01a0cace-ecd7-7355-b1db-e3dafa507991\"],\n      \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"c963b0b0-1108-7ea7-940d-01123d9cc020\", \"7af22950-46db-75ef-a410-7afe128a90aa\", \"d0c0e6db-3dc0-7132-80b1-b30a86bfb826\"],\n      \"estimatedSeconds\": 35\n    },\n    {\n      \"kind\": \"concept\",\n      \"title\": \"Tzedakah: Three Dimensions of Righteousness\",\n      \"description\": \"Explore the Hebrew word Tzedakah and its three inseparable ramifications: personal morality (internal rectitude), justice (structural fairness), and charity/generosity (giving as justice, not optional benevolence).\",\n      \"objectiveIds\": [\"01a0cace-ecd7-7970-8683-661a513bb105\"],\n      \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"06034497-9561-73ab-9a48-7e0b4dd07526\", \"74a62c36-c225-74cd-ab8b-4c70bfa21c0c\", \"fe3027da-43fa-7c54-abee-645434318ebe\", \"49c29e8f-988b-7974-8e1c-98507766b8dc\"],\n      \"estimatedSeconds\": 30\n    },\n ","textChunks":["\n{\n  \"schemaVersion\": \"outline-v1\",\n  \"targetDurationSeconds\": 180,\n  \"items\": [\n    {\n      \"kind\": \"hook\",\n      \"title\": \"The 50/30/20 Challenge\",\n      \"description\": \"Open with a provocative question: 'If you received 20 million naira today, would you know exactly how to allocate it using the 50/30/20 rule, or would you simply make more expensive mistakes?' This frames the lesson's exploration of financial stewardship and Kingdom Economics.\",\n      \"objectiveIds\": [\"01a0cace-ecd7-7239-afef-9a0413bb4e1c\"],\n      \"sourceBlockIds\": [],\n      \"estimatedSeconds\": 25,\n      \"framingNote\": \"Generated framing device to engage learners by connecting the abstract concept of stewardship to a concrete financial scenario. Not directly sourced from the material.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"kind\": \"concept\",\n      \"title\": \"Righteousness: Gift vs. Harvest\",\n      \"description\": \"Distinguish between positional righteousness (a fixed gift received by grace through faith) and practical righteousness (the harvest of visible works that can be multiplied). Explain why both must be active in a believer's life to avoid doctrinal imbalance.\",\n      \"objectiveIds\": [\"01a0cace-ecd7-7355-b1db-e3dafa507991\"],\n      \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"c963b0b0-1108-7ea7-940d-01123d9cc020\", \"7af22950-46db-75ef-a410-7afe128a90aa\", \"d0c0e6db-3dc0-7132-80b1-b30a86bfb826\"],\n      \"estimatedSeconds\": 35\n    },\n    {\n      \"kind\": \"concept\",\n      \"title\": \"Tzedakah: Three Dimensions of Righteousness\",\n      \"description\": \"Explore the Hebrew word Tzedakah and its three inseparable ramifications: personal morality (internal rectitude), justice (structural fairness), and charity/generosity (giving as justice, not optional benevolence).\",\n      \"objectiveIds\": [\"01a0cace-ecd7-7970-8683-661a513bb105\"],\n      \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"06034497-9561-73ab-9a48-7e0b4dd07526\", \"74a62c36-c225-74cd-ab8b-4c70bfa21c0c\", \"fe3027da-43fa-7c54-abee-645434318ebe\", \"49c29e8f-988b-7974-8e1c-98507766b8dc\"],\n      \"estimatedSeconds\": 30\n    },\n ","   {\n      \"kind\": \"example\",\n      \"title\": \"Kingdom Economics in Practice\",\n      \"description\": \"Examine three specific Biblical economic practices: returning a debtor's cloak before sundown (fairness over legal rights), periodic debt cancellation (Jubilee), and leaving gleanings for the poor. Explain how each protects the vulnerable from exploitation.\",\n      \"objectiveIds\": [\"01a0cace-ecd7-7b8d-9e03-abc39630db01\"],\n      \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"b29eff38-6707-7ec8-9cc2-3acf8b734309\", \"23d224bd-1662-7e5a-93b1-c26aa4216531\", \"f1f0308a-70b9-7c61-bf74-93a6bf2ad067\", \"a8294542-be65-7173-89e6-421f1913a466\"],\n      \"estimatedSeconds\": 30\n    },\n    {\n      \"kind\": \"analogy\",\n      \"title\": \"Power vs. Wisdom: Jethro and Mark 5\",\n      \"description\": \"Compare Moses' need for Jethro's structural wisdom to sustain his miraculous power with Jesus commanding nourishment for Jairus's daughter after her resurrection. Illustrate that power produces miracles, but wisdom sustains them; without wisdom, what is built will burn out or die again.\",\n      \"objectiveIds\": [\"01a0cace-ecd7-7a1a-9412-52d954644606\"],\n      \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"afe140a5-8141-7709-8e11-8dfb41acef12\", \"44fdb66c-c888-7231-9e57-293f33c4efea\", \"2f2a6065-ab09-75d0-b83d-f382b614cf54\"],\n      \"estimatedSeconds\": 30\n    },\n    {\n      \"kind\": \"concept\",\n      \"title\": \"The Five Pillars and 50/30/20 Budgeting\",\n      \"description\": \"Introduce the five pillars of financial stewardship (Budgeting, Protection, Savings, Investment, Debt Management) and explain the 50/30/20 allocation rule: 50% for needs, 30% for wants, and 20% for savings/investment. Demonstrate how to calculate a sample budget using this formula.\",\n      \"objectiveIds\": [\"01a0cace-ecd7-7239-afef-9a0413bb4e1c\"],\n      \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"f95b27d2-c234-738f-87ee-cf404117fd5a\", \"d8d10398-fc31-7207-8067-7d205b09e480\", \"dd8e865f-a031-7bdc-8f60-67cddffe293f\", \"19c878fa-239b-717b-b639-679449af7ad3\", \"7a32b18c-fe32-715f-b6f2-3ef07a0836cf\", \"66e311a8-add0-7a1d-8ef6-0","93444c88a60\", \"09df5ee4-b668-7289-9457-76279f00717b\"],\n      \"estimatedSeconds\": 30\n    },\n    {\n      \"kind\": \"example\",\n      \"title\": \"The Parable of the Talents: Accountability\",\n      \"description\": \"Compare the outcomes of the servants with five, two, and one talents. Explain that the one-talent servant was condemned not for having less, but for making zero interest and showing no growth, demonstrating that stewardship requires faithfulness regardless of the amount.\",\n      \"objectiveIds\": [\"01a0cace-ecd7-7bc6-ae8b-1812d9d98dc6\"],\n      \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"49ec6ab8-4041-757d-8594-ceb5170b4b8e\"],\n      \"estimatedSeconds\": 20\n    },\n    {\n      \"kind\": \"summary\",\n      \"title\": \"Stewardship: Integrating Righteousness and Wisdom\",\n      \"description\": \"Recap the journey from understanding righteousness as both gift and harvest, through the practical ethics of Tzedakah and Kingdom Economics, to the necessity of wisdom following power, and finally to the practical application of the five pillars and 50/30/20 budgeting as our stewardship test.\",\n      \"objectiveIds\": [\"01a0cace-ecd7-7355-b1db-e3dafa507991\", \"01a0cace-ecd7-7970-8683-661a513bb105\", \"01a0cace-ecd7-7b8d-9e03-abc39630db01\", \"01a0cace-ecd7-7a1a-9412-52d954644606\", \"01a0cace-ecd7-7239-afef-9a0413bb4e1c\", \"01a0cace-ecd7-7bc6-ae8b-1812d9d98dc6\"],\n      \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"c963b0b0-1108-7ea7-940d-01123d9cc020\", \"44fdb66c-c888-7231-9e57-293f33c4efea\", \"49ec6ab8-4041-757d-8594-ceb5170b4b8e\", \"dd8e865f-a031-7bdc-8f60-67cddffe293f\"],\n      \"estimatedSeconds\": 10\n    }\n  ]\n}\n"],"textChunksTruncated":false,"textCharacters":5553,"reasoningCharacters":0,"finishReason":"stop","inputTokens":"[REDACTED]","outputTokens":"[REDACTED]"},"retries":0,"latencyMs":19537,"service":"pipeline-worker","correlationId":"01a0cad2-8800-77e4-869b-80f2d961b171"}}
